# TODO - Ahead-of-execution native translation

## Objective

Make verified ahead-of-execution translation the primary native path. Use
the portable execution IR between Malbolge decode and architecture-specific code
generation, then build or load exact native artifacts before guest execution
from reachable code-state evidence. When verification proves a finite closed
self-modification graph, compile its reachable code-state variants ahead of time
and lower runtime self-modification to guarded transitions among those already
compiled variants.

Offline CPU, GPU, or superoptimization search may propose stronger reductions,
but independent deterministic verification remains the only admission authority.
Regions that cannot be proven safe fall back to ordinary VM execution.

- Process-local preparation transactionally compiles requested direct fast
  paths,
  deduplicates exact artifact keys, rejects empty/deoptimization-only or failed
  variants, and publishes only a complete sealed
  VerifiedAheadOfExecutionNativeSet.
- Runtime AOT lookup never emits on a miss and distinguishes exact hit,
  uncovered identity, and unsupported host format after profile preflight.
- Ordered direct sequences require every exact step to exist in the sealed set;
  partial AOT coverage publishes no sequence plan and mutates nothing.
- Finite exact-state graph claims are replayed through ProfileMachine before
  admission. Portable IR must reproject exactly, continued edges must land on
  the complete claimed successor checkpoint, and closed/reachable topology is
  required before all graph-node fast paths are prepared into one sealed set.
- Register-masked v6 portable IR now has transactional object-only AOT
  preparation and read-only lookup. Exact mask-aware keys are deduplicated and
  every object is independently verified before the sealed set is published.
- Verifier-admitted research regions now expose their product-owned v6 effect
  IR for an explicit handoff into ordinary native admission. Integration
  evidence proves a reviewed one-step region may prepare AOT while a verified
  multi-step
  reduction remains fail-closed until a matching native shape exists. Product
  multi-step reprojection now derives dependency masks from normative traces and
  rejects continuity/profile/outcome drift plus unrepresented derived geometry.
- Durable artifact loading, reduced graph topology handoff, runtime native
  transition dispatch, and verified collapsed multi-step effects remain open.

## Acceptance

- Only regions whose code-state assumptions are explicit may be compiled before
  execution, and cache keys include every assumption required for safe native
  reuse.
- A verifier-proven finite closed state graph may be materialized as precompiled
  native code-state variants with explicit transitions; no runtime mutation may
  silently select a variant absent from the admitted graph.
- A native transition may collapse multiple guest steps only when
  deterministic verification proves the complete net effect on registers,
  memory, I/O, termination, and every retained code-state dependency.
- Offline CPU/GPU/superoptimization output is untrusted proposal material until
  deterministic verification proves the claimed state effect and cache identity.
- No fixed speedup is an acceptance criterion. Benchmarks must separate offline
  preparation cost, artifact load cost, transition overhead, and steady-state
  execution from interpreter and JIT baselines.
- Observable state, I/O, termination, and diagnostics match the declared
  semantic profile across positive, boundary, and adversarial fixtures.
- Performance conclusions use equivalent workloads and report raw-sample
  provenance, resource budgets, dispersion/uncertainty, and failure/success
  behavior rather than only a best-case number.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `vm/`, `execution/`, `tests/vm/`,
  `benchmarks/interpreter/`.
- Required evidence: semantic fixtures, state/I/O traces where diagnostic, and
  differential results against independent interpreter-compatible
  implementations; the original C source is compared only where its behavior is
  defined and reproducible.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `tiered-native-execution-engine`,
